        "answer": {
          "short": "(i) $\\sqrt{14}$\n(ii) $\\frac12$\n(iii) $4+\\sqrt{14}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=(2-\\sqrt3)^2+(2+\\sqrt3)^2\\\\x^2&=(7-4\\sqrt3)+(7+4\\sqrt3)\\\\x^2&=14\\\\x&=\\sqrt{14}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(2-\\sqrt3)(2+\\sqrt3)\\\\A&=\\frac12(4-3)\\\\A&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=(2-\\sqrt3)+(2+\\sqrt3)+\\sqrt{14}\\\\P&=4+\\sqrt{14}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
